resource: a placed buffer may sit at any offset the buffer minimum allows (NutsEmu)

A placed buffer is a slice of its heap's own buffer, so its offset only has to meet the buffer
minimum (256 bytes), not the 64 KB placement alignment. Subnautica 2 (Unreal Engine 5) placed a
1808-byte UAV buffer off the 64 KB alignment in a default heap, got E_INVALIDARG from
CreatePlacedResource and ended with a fatal error as it loaded (2026-10-20). The first such
buffer is logged with its offset; textures, and buffers off the 256-byte minimum, are still
refused, now with an ERR saying why.

